<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan approves opening of Belgian bank branch.</title>
<headline>Taiwan approves opening of Belgian bank branch.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's finance ministry said on Tuesday it has agreed to let Belgian-based Generale Bank set up a branch office on the island, bringing to 46 the number of foreign banks in Taiwan.</p>
<p>The Generale Bank, capitalised at US$4.521 billion and ranked the world's 78th biggest bank, has had a Taiwan representative office since 1994, a ministry statement said.</p>
<p>It is the biggest bank in Belgium, with 1,100 domestic and 10 overseas branches as well as 14 representative offices.</p>
